    thinking: "**Considering User Needs**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s request: to integrate a mini-map view showing registered store locations on either the list or detail screens. I\'ll need to consider how to handle Google Map links as starting points, ensuring user convenience is prioritized in this implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Map Functionality**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating a mini-map view, and the latest focus is the **SpotDetailModal**. I plan to use Google Maps Embed, based on a Google Maps link or the store name and area, for an interactive preview. I\'m also including a navigation button to open Google Maps directly. For the list screen, I\'m leaning toward a toggle for a \"card view\" versus \"map view\" mode to plot and display all registered locations.\n\n\n**Refining Map Integration**\n\nI\'ve just added `SpotMiniMapView.tsx`, enabling mini pop-up cards on pin clicks, which then open the detail modal. I\'ve also incorporated color-coding for \"unvisited,\" \"visited,\" and \"favorite\" statuses. Direct links to Google Maps for each spot are now supported. Furthermore, I\'ve added a \"Access Mini Map\" section to the detail modal, displaying Google Maps directly from a link or location data, complete with buttons to open the Google Maps app and launch navigation. I am now working on plotting map views for the list screen, starting with coordinates for major Tokyo areas.\n\n\n**Evaluating Map Technologies**\n\nI am now assessing mapping technology options. I\'m considering using Leaflet with OpenStreetMap tiles to offer a zoomable, interactive experience, and I might pair that with Google Maps embeds for detailed views. I\342\200\231m also looking to parse Google Maps URLs to extract queries or infer coordinates from location names. I\'ve confirmed that `leaflet` isn\'t installed, and I\'ll need to install it with `@types/leaflet`.\n\n\n"
