  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reimagining GourmetShare**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user experience. The goal is a visual transformation, moving away from a traditional restaurant database feel. I\'m aiming for a Pinterest/Lemon8/Kinfolk-inspired curated lifestyle experience. It needs to be less sterile and more engaging. I\'m exploring the visual impact of incorporating curated editorial lifestyle images to enhance the overall aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining Discover Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user journey, specifically the \"Discover\" flow. I\'m prioritizing \"Who recommended it\" and \"What they said about it\" as GourmetShare\'s core value. This will be achieved by prominently featuring authentic quotes. I\'m envisioning a rich visual mood that leans into editorial photography to create an emotional connection. I\'m also planning a blend of clean, practical list/grid views for comparison, and spot details with essential info and actionable buttons. The goal is a natural flow from discovery to save/visit/memo.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 258458053
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
